# Sunrise demo: a 2-minute wake-up ramp using RGB colour commands only.
# It starts at deep red (ff0000, brightness 1), passes through orange (ff3c00 at 30%,
# ff7a14 at 60%) and amber (ffa648 at 85%), and ends at a warm white (ffb060,
# brightness 100). A colour command turns a light that is off on by itself, and the
# light stays on at full brightness at the end; there is no final off.
# Generated with blemeshctl.timers.sunrise_program_text(120). For a real alarm, use
# 'blemeshctl sunrise --at 07:00 --over 30m', which runs the same ramp unattended.
color ff0000 1
wait 5s
color ff0800 4
wait 5s
color ff1100 6
wait 5s
color ff1900 9
wait 5s
color ff2100 12
wait 5s
color ff2a00 14
wait 5s
color ff3200 17
wait 5s
color ff3a00 19
wait 5s
color ff4302 24
wait 5s
color ff4c05 29
wait 5s
color ff5408 34
wait 5s
color ff5d0b 38
wait 5s
color ff650d 43
wait 5s
color ff6e10 48
wait 5s
color ff7713 53
wait 5s
color ff7e19 58
wait 5s
color ff8622 63
wait 5s
color ff8d2b 68
wait 5s
color ff9433 73
wait 5s
color ff9c3c 78
wait 5s
color ffa345 83
wait 5s
color ffa84c 88
wait 5s
color ffaa53 92
wait 5s
color ffad59 96
wait 5s
color ffb060 100
